[Term]
id: CHEBI:15854
name: quinine
def: "A cinchona alkaloid that is cinchonidine in which the hydrogen at the 6-position of the quinoline ring is substituted by methoxy." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:16015
name: L-glutamic acid
def: "An optically active form of glutamic acid having <small>L</small>-configuration." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:16226
name: limonin

[Term]
id: CHEBI:17992
name: sucrose
def: "A glycosyl glycoside formed by glucose and fructose units joined by an acetal oxygen bridge from hemiacetal of glucose to the hemiketal of the fructose." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:26710
name: sodium chloride
def: "An inorganic chloride salt having sodium(1+) as the counterion." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:27732
name: caffeine
def: "A trimethylxanthine in which the three methyl groups are located at positions 1, 3, and 7. A purine alkaloid that occurs naturally in tea and coffee." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:28775
name: hesperidin
def: "A disaccharide derivative that consists of hesperetin substituted by a 6-<em>O</em>-(α-<small>L</small>-rhamnopyranosyl)-β-<small>D</small>-glucopyranosyl moiety at position 7 via a glycosidic linkage." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:28819
name: naringin
def: "A disaccharide derivative that is (<i>S</i>)-naringenin substituted by a 2-<em>O</em>-(α-<small>L</small>-rhamnopyranosyl)-β-<small>D</small>-glucopyranosyl moiety at position 7 via a glycosidic linkage." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:30769
name: citric acid
def: "A tricarboxylic acid that is propane-1,2,3-tricarboxylic acid bearing a hydroxy substituent at position 2. It is an important metabolite in the pathway of all aerobic organisms." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:46261
name: N-phenylthiourea
def: "A member of the class of thioureas that is thiourea in which one of the hydrogens is replaced by a phenyl group. Depending on their genetic makeup, humans find it either very bitter-tasting or tasteless. This unusual property resulted in <em>N</em>-phenylthiourea being used in paternity testing prior to the advent of DNA testing." []

[Term]
id: CHEBI:8502
name: 6-propyl-2-thiouracil
def: "A pyrimidinethione consisting of uracil in which the 2-oxo group is substituted by a thio group and the hydrogen at position 6 is substituted by a propyl group." []

[Term]
id: CL:0000209
name: taste receptor cell
def: "A specialized cell involved in gustatory sensory perception." []

[Term]
id: FOODON:00003027
name: pomelo fruit
def: "A whole fruit of a pomelo tree (Citrus maximus)" []

[Term]
id: FOODON:00003324
name: citrus fruit
def: "A hesperidium fruit of a citrus plant (Citrus)." []

[Term]
id: FOODON:00003554
name: grapefruit
def: "A hesperidium fruit of a grapefruit tree (Citrus x paradisi)." []

[Term]
id: FOODON:00003555
name: mandarin orange
def: "A hesperidium fruit of a mandarin orange tree (Citrus reticulata)." []

[Term]
id: FOODON:00003732
name: yuzu
def: "A hesperidium fruit of a yuzu plant (Citrus junos)" []

[Term]
id: FOODON:03301103
name: orange juice
def: "SIREN DB annotation: * liquid, low viscosity, with small particles FOODON:03430114 * fruit, peel removed, core, pit or seed removed FOODON:03420229" []

[Term]
id: FOODON:03305428
name: lemon juice
def: "SIREN DB annotation: * liquid, low viscosity FOODON:03430109 * fruit, peel present, core, pit or seed present FOODON:03420140" []

[Term]
id: FOODON:03305742
name: citrus juice
def: "SIREN DB annotation: * liquid, low viscosity FOODON:03430109 * fruit, peel present, core, pit or seed present FOODON:03420140" []

[Term]
id: GO:0001580
name: detection of chemical stimulus involved in sensory perception of bitter taste
def: "The series of events required for a bitter taste stimulus to be received and converted to a molecular signal." []

[Term]
id: GO:0008150
name: biological_process
def: "Note that, in addition to forming the root of the biological process ontology, this term is recommended for the annotation of gene products whose biological process is unknown. When this term is used for annotation, it indicates that no information was available about the biological process of the gene product annotated as of the date the annotation was made; the evidence code 'no data' (ND), is used to indicate this." []

[Term]
id: GO:0008527
name: taste receptor activity
def: "Combining with soluble compounds to initiate a change in cell activity. These receptors are responsible for the sense of taste." []

[Term]
id: GO:0033038
name: bitter taste receptor activity
def: "Combining with soluble bitter compounds to initiate a change in cell activity. These receptors are responsible for the sense of bitter taste." []

[Term]
id: GO:0050909
name: sensory perception of taste
def: "The series of events required for an organism to receive a gustatory stimulus, convert it to a molecular signal, and recognize and characterize the signal. Gustation involves the direct detection of chemical composition, usually through contact with chemoreceptor cells. This is a neurological process." []

[Term]
id: GO:0050913
name: sensory perception of bitter taste
def: "The series of events required to receive a bitter taste stimulus, convert it to a molecular signal, and recognize and characterize the signal. This is a neurological process." []

[Term]
id: GO:0050914
name: sensory perception of salty taste
def: "The series of events required to receive a salty taste stimulus, convert it to a molecular signal, and recognize and characterize the signal. This is a neurological process." []

[Term]
id: GO:0050915
name: sensory perception of sour taste
def: "The series of events required to receive a sour taste stimulus, convert it to a molecular signal, and recognize and characterize the signal. This is a neurological process." []

[Term]
id: GO:0050916
name: sensory perception of sweet taste
def: "The series of events required to receive a sweet taste stimulus, convert it to a molecular signal, and recognize and characterize the signal. This is a neurological process." []

[Term]
id: GO:0050917
name: sensory perception of umami taste
def: "The series of events required to receive an umami taste stimulus, convert it to a molecular signal, and recognize and characterize the signal. Umami taste is the savory taste of meats and other foods that are rich in glutamates. This is a neurological process." []

[Term]
id: GO:0090682
name: GPCR bitter taste receptor activity
def: "A G protein-coupled receptor activity that is responsible for the sense of bitter taste." []

[Term]
id: HP:0000223
name: Abnormality of taste sensation

[Term]
id: HP:0000224
name: Hypogeusia
def: "A decreased ability to perceive flavor." []

[Term]
id: HP:0031249
name: Parageusia
def: "A distortion of the sense of taste, often characterized by the sensation of a metallic taste." []

[Term]
id: HP:0041051
name: Ageusia
def: "A rare condition that is characterized by a complete loss of taste function of the tongue." []

[Term]
id: HTO:0000001
name: tasting event
def: "A planned process in which a human taster orally samples a stimulus and reports one or more perceived taste qualities." []
is_a: OBI:0000070 ! assay
property_value: IAO:0000119 "HTO:0000000" xsd:string

[Term]
id: IAO:0000030
name: information content entity
def: "A generically dependent continuant that is about some thing." []

[Term]
id: IAO:0000032
name: scalar measurement datum
def: "A scalar measurement datum is a measurement datum that is composed of two parts, numerals and a unit label." []

[Term]
id: IAO:0000109
name: measurement datum
def: "A measurement datum is an information content entity that is a recording of the output of a measurement such as produced by a device." []

[Term]
id: OBA:VT0001986
name: taste sensitivity trait
def: "The sensitivity toward of a sensory perception of taste." []

[Term]
id: OBA:VT0004209
name: sweet taste sensitivity trait
def: "The quality of a sensory perception of sweet taste." []

[Term]
id: OBA:VT0004210
name: bitter taste sensitivity trait
def: "The quality of a sensory perception of bitter taste." []

[Term]
id: OBA:VT0004211
name: sour taste sensitivity trait
def: "The quality of a sensory perception of sour taste." []

[Term]
id: OBA:VT0004212
name: salty taste sensitivity trait
def: "The quality of a sensory perception of salty taste." []

[Term]
id: OBA:VT0004213
name: umami taste sensitivity trait
def: "The quality of a sensory perception of umami taste." []

[Term]
id: OBI:0000070
name: assay
def: "A planned process that has the objective to produce information about a material entity (the evaluant) by examining it." []

[Term]
id: OBI:0001000
name: questionnaire
def: "A document with a set of printed or written questions with a choice of answers, devised for the purposes of a survey or statistical study." []

[Term]
id: PATO:0000001
name: quality
def: "A dependent entity that inheres in a bearer by virtue of how the bearer is related to other entities" []

[Term]
id: PATO:0000049
name: intensity
def: "A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's possessing or displaying a distinctive feature in type or degree or effect or force." []

[Term]
id: PATO:0001241
name: physical object quality
def: "Relational qualities are qualities that hold between multiple entities. Normal (monadic) qualities such as the shape of a eyeball exist purely as a quality of that eyeball. A relational quality such as sensitivity to light is a quality of that eyeball (and connecting nervous system) as it relates to incoming light waves/particles." []

[Term]
id: PATO:0001309
name: duration
def: "A process quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's magnitude of the temporal extent between the starting and ending point." []

[Term]
id: PATO:0002325
name: onset quality
def: "The temporal relation between the start of the process with respect to a reference process." []

[Term]
id: PATO:0002474
name: bitter
def: "A flavor quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an acrid, sharp, or disagreeable flavor." []

[Term]
id: UBERON:0000167
name: oral cavity
def: "Anatomical cavity at the start of the digestive tract that that is enclosed by the mouth. The boundaries and contents vary depending on the species. In vertebrates, the boundaries are the oral opening, the cheeks, the palate and (if present) the palatoglossal arch - if this is not present then the mouth and pharynx form the oropharyngeal cavity. The buccal cavity contains the teeth, tongue and palate (when present)." []

[Term]
id: UBERON:0001723
name: tongue
def: "A muscular organ in the floor of the mouth." []

[Term]
id: UBERON:0001727
name: taste bud
def: "A specialized receptor organ that is a collection of cells spanning the gustatory epithelium." []

[Term]
id: UBERON:0002448
name: fungiform papilla
def: "Any of the mushroom-shaped papillae, which have a single taste bud at the tip, located mostly on the dorsal anterior portion of the tongue." []

